# Trust-root paths. A path is owned when its content reaches a privileged context:
# (a) it runs or loads in a job that holds a secret or the standards-sync environment,
#     or in a Claude lane that restores it from main before running;
# (b) the sync copies it into other repositories at an executable or trust-bearing path;
# (c) it decides what the sync distributes;
# (d) it is policy that gates merges or runner routing;
# (e) it is a workflow, an action, or this file.
# The trust-root ruleset requires an approving review from a code owner listed here
# before a change to these paths merges. Paths not listed have no owner and need no
# code-owner review. The last matching entry wins; an entry with no owner unowns the path.

